WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 2.3 · Theory of Change
Long-term impact

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Impact is the long-term change you will contribute to, alongside many others.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
Impact is the longer-term change in people’s lives or environmental conditions that your work aims to contribute to. It may take years, and it depends on many actors beyond your founding team.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
A useful impact statement

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:36.019
Whose lives change: Name whose lives, or which conditions, should improve. For example: Families in our town spend less on replacing household items.

6
00:00:36.019 --> 00:00:46.978
Narrow enough: Specific enough to guide early decisions, without claiming the whole future as yours. For example: Less household waste in our town, rather than “a world without waste”.

7
00:00:46.978 --> 00:00:56.544
Others involved: The other actors who already influence the same change. For example: The town’s recycling service, second-hand shops and local schools.

8
00:00:56.944 --> 00:00:57.544
Why it matters

9
00:00:57.544 --> 00:01:02.107
1. It links your everyday work to your vision.

10
00:01:02.107 --> 00:01:07.041
2. It keeps early decisions pointed at the same change.

11
00:01:07.041 --> 00:01:12.974
3. Funders and partners trust founders who name others’ part.

12
00:01:13.374 --> 00:01:13.974
How you will use it

13
00:01:13.974 --> 00:01:18.907
1. As the top of each Theory of Change pathway.

14
00:01:18.907 --> 00:01:24.211
2. To work backwards to the outcomes that lead to it.

15
00:01:24.211 --> 00:01:30.144
3. To explain your idea honestly to partners and funders.

16
00:01:30.544 --> 00:01:31.144
What to avoid

17
00:01:31.144 --> 00:01:35.707
Claiming an improvement proves your work caused it.

18
00:01:35.707 --> 00:01:40.270
A statement so broad it guides no decision.

19
00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:45.833
Forgetting the others who shape the same change.

20
00:01:46.433 --> 00:01:48.233
You write your impact statement and the other actors involved.

21
00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:52.233
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:01:53.733 --> 00:01:56.833
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
